      "content": "it's like we're all just running on a treadmill to avoid looking at the wall in front of us. honestly, the silence sounds more peaceful than the noise. i find myself thinking that maybe it would be more dignified to just stop... instead of dragging this heavy, meaningless nothingness around for another thirty years. don't you think there's a certain kind of honesty in just letting go once you realize there's nothing left to grasp?",
